{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Command Log.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Command Log.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender command log blender command log","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Command Log.md","fileName":"Blender Command Log.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Command Log","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 09:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Python Scripting Environment]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Python Scripting Environment","Blender Interactive Console","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Command Log.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Command Log.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender command log blender command log","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Command Log.md","fileName":"Blender Command Log.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Command Log","heading":"Blender Command Log","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The Blender Command Log records Python operator calls generated by many actions in the graphical interface. Moving an object, for example, exposes a corresponding `bpy.ops.transform` call, giving the developer a concrete starting point for automation without first memorizing the API.\n\nRecorded calls often contain interface-state arguments that are unnecessary in a reusable script. A productive workflow copies the call into the [[Blender Interactive Console]], removes optional details, and tests the smallest expression that preserves the intended result. The log is therefore a discovery aid, not automatically finished program code.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Python Scripting Environment","Blender Interactive Console","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF